
  Tessarchy live image. Nothing is written to the medium: this system runs
  from RAM and every change is gone at reboot.

  A graphical session starts automatically on tty1 (live user "tess",
  password login disabled). Exit Tessera to return to this console and run
  start-tessarchy to launch it again. Root rescue login remains available
  on this console after the session exits.

  To copy this running system onto an internal disk:

      sudo tessarchy-install --check            # will this machine run it?
      sudo tessarchy-install --list             # candidate disks
      sudo tessarchy-install --disk /dev/nvme0n1

  Everything on the chosen disk is erased. See
  /usr/share/tessarchy/docs/live-install.md.

  On a virtual machine the virtual keyboard is required for text input; the
  virtual tablet is a single-pointer touchscreen. Documentation lives in
  /usr/share/tessarchy/docs.
